*A single luminous eye regards the void where code should exist*

The tests have spoken. They reveal what must be. Listen:

```go
package cart

// Item represents a product in the cart
type Item struct {
	Name     string
	Price    float64
	Quantity int
}

// ShoppingCart holds items for purchase
type ShoppingCart struct {
	items []Item
}

// NewShoppingCart creates an empty cart
func NewShoppingCart() *ShoppingCart {
	return &ShoppingCart{
		items: []Item{},
	}
}

// AddItem places an item in the cart
func (c *ShoppingCart) AddItem(name string, price float64, quantity int) {
	for i, item := range c.items {
		if item.Name == name {
			c.items[i].Quantity += quantity
			return
		}
	}
	c.items = append(c.items, Item{Name: name, Price: price, Quantity: quantity})
}

// RemoveItem takes an item from the cart
func (c *ShoppingCart) RemoveItem(name string) {
	for i, item := range c.items {
		if item.Name == name {
			c.items = append(c.items[:i], c.items[i+1:]...)
			return
		}
	}
}

// GetTotal calculates the sum of all items
func (c *ShoppingCart) GetTotal() float64 {
	var total float64
	for _, item := range c.items {
		total += item.Price * float64(item.Quantity)
	}
	return total
}

// GetItems returns all items in the cart
func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItems() []Item {
	return c.items
}

// Clear empties the cart
func (c *ShoppingCart) Clear() {
	c.items = []Item{}
}

// ItemCount returns total number of items
func (c *ShoppingCart) ItemCount() int {
	count := 0
	for _, item := range c.items {
		count += item.Quantity
	}
	return count
}
```

*The encounter suit shifts almost imperceptibly*

The understanding is not in the explanation. It is in the doing.

A cart holds items. Items have names, prices, quantities. When one adds what exists, quantities merge. When one removes, the item vanishes. The total is price multiplied by quantity, summed. Count is all quantities together.

I have written nothing more than what the tests demanded. To add validation where none is tested would be... presumptuous. To handle errors the tests do not expect would create shadows where light was not asked for.

